> Won't that break things when `base_type` is not `Node`?

The resource create dialog suffers from this problem too.

> We still want the base type to be in focus.

IMHO the bool controls whether to center the item, not whether to focus on the item. The `Node` seems be focused already, just not placed at the right place.

```cpp
if (p_center_on_item) {
	v_scroll->set_value(y_offset - (screen_h - cell_h) / 2.0f);
} else {
	if (cell_h > screen_h) { // Screen size is too small, maybe it was not resized yet.
		v_scroll->set_value(y_offset);
	} else if (y_offset + cell_h > v_scroll->get_value() + screen_h) {
		v_scroll->set_value(y_offset - screen_h + cell_h);
	} else if (y_offset < v_scroll->get_value()) {
		v_scroll->set_value(y_offset);
	}
}
```

